// The data cache in front of the wait-state window (RV32 region soc_pkg::RV_REGION_XMEM):
// direct-mapped, write-back and write-allocate, 8-word lines, soc_pkg::DCACHE_LINES (64)
// lines (2 KB). It sits between the CPU's data accesses (RV32 MEM_WAIT; Hack's M reads and
// writes, in its D segment) and soc_xmem_bridge's data side, which sees only line
// transfers: a write-back and a fill, each 8 one-word requests.
// - Lines are keyed by the PSRAM word (addr[22:2]: line [10:5], word [4:2], tag [22:11]),
//   so every alias of a word in region 8 is the same line, as the memory behind the window
//   repeats every 8 MB. Hack's data word A is in line A[8:3].
// - tags (LUT RAM, {valid, dirty, tag}) and words (one 512x36 block RAM, {mask[3:0],
//   data}) are read a cycle ahead at rd_idx (the CPU's data_addr: the access address,
//   computed in EXECUTE and held through MEM_WAIT), as the ROM is. In MEM_WAIT the registered
//   tag is compared with data_addr (the registered access address). The probe has a second,
//   asynchronous read port on tags (ptag), so it adds no cycle to an instruction miss.
// - A hit (in IDLE, the read-ahead at this access's word, not stale) completes in its
//   cycle: a load returns word_q, which is all rdata ever is (the bridge's word never
//   reaches the CPU); a store merges its bytes into the word, ORs its strobes into the
//   word's mask and marks the line dirty, with no bus access. Loads and stores cost what a
//   load of the ROM costs.
// - A miss (also of a partial store: write-allocate) leaves IDLE: to WB if the victim line is
//   valid and dirty, else to FILL. WB writes the victim's 8 words back (mem_we, mem_wstrb =
//   the word's mask: only the bytes the CPU stored reach the PSRAM, so a byte the cache
//   never had defined, X in simulation, is never written; the W955 model counts an
//   unmasked X byte as an error). FILL reads the access's 8 words, each written as
//   {4'b0000, word}, then the tag {1, 0, tag}, and returns to IDLE. The access then
//   completes as a hit, two cycles later (the next cycle is stale: the tag and word are
//   read again at rd_idx).
// - The word counter cnt advances with the bridge's ready (mem_ready while mem_sel: the
//   response); it wraps to 0 after the eighth word, so it is 0 in IDLE. In WB the word RAM
//   is read at {line, cnt_next} instead of rd_idx (the select is the registered state), so
//   the first WB cycle only reads word 0 and raises no request.
// - mem_sel is high in FILL and, from its second cycle, in WB: only while a request is
//   wanted, and never dropped under one in flight. The fields (mem_we, mem_addr = {tag,
//   line, cnt} from registers, mem_wdata/mem_wstrb = word_q, which holds word cnt) stay
//   unchanged until the response: the RAMs aren't written in WB.
// - Cycle costs over a hit, with the controller's latencies R (soc_pkg::XMEM_READ_LATENCY,
//   35) and W (XMEM_WRITE_LATENCY, 34), each request taken in the cycle it is raised and
//   the next one raised the cycle after the response (sim/unit/test_soc_dcache.py
//   measures them): a miss with an invalid or clean victim 8(R+1)+2 = 290; with a dirty
//   victim 8(W+1)+8(R+1)+3 = 571. A stale or mismatched read-ahead adds a cycle.
// - The probe: an instruction-cache miss (probe_req) at the PSRAM word probe_addr (soc_top's
//   win_fetch_addr, from pc_reg, never pc_out) whose line this cache holds valid and dirty
//   with the same tag (probe_dirty, combinational from ptag; soc_icache's fill_hold, which
//   keeps its miss from the bridge) starts a write-back in IDLE when no data access is in
//   the window (data first; none is in MEM_WAIT while the CPU fetches): the line is
//   written back as on a dirty miss and stays valid, now clean ({1, 0, tag}); probe_dirty
//   falls the cycle after the last word's response and the instruction cache's request
//   follows. A probed miss costs 8(W+1)+2 = 282 cycles before the fetch's own R: 317. The
//   words keep their masks: a later write-back of the line writes those bytes again,
//   unchanged. Without a dirty match the probe costs nothing (the miss stays R = 35).
// - soc_xmem_bridge's contract (its header): data_sel must not rise while the fetch's
//   request waits for req_ready. A line transfer starts either in MEM_WAIT (the
//   instruction's fetch completed) or by the probe, whose fill_hold keeps the instruction
//   cache from requesting, so the bridge is always free when mem_sel rises.
// - A write to the address being read in the same cycle leaves that read undefined on the
//   board (-no-rw-check; RTL simulation shows the old value). stale_q, high the cycle after
//   such a collision (the tag line or the word) and the cycle after any cycle outside
//   IDLE, makes that cycle a non-lookup: the access waits a cycle, rd_idx being held.
//   Writes happen in a store hit's cycle, in FILL, at the end of a probe's write-back and
//   in the sweep.
// - Hack's instruction that reads M and writes it (AM=M+1) loads in MEM_WAIT and stores the
//   whole word from the next cycle (HACK_WB), rd_idx at the same word all along. The load
//   completes as a hit, a cycle with no write (a miss completes by the replay), so the
//   store's lookup is not stale and it hits: AM=M+1 costs the load's cycles only.
// - clear (high while soc_top's power-on reset counts) invalidates every line once, one a
//   cycle (64 cycles), before the CPU runs: the RAMs have no reset. Until then window
//   accesses wait and the probe sees nothing. The words aren't cleared: a line is filled
//   before any of its words is used, which clears the masks.
// - rst is soc_top's rst_n (power-on and the reset button): it resets the FSM, possibly in
//   the middle of a transfer, and the sweep that follows drops the dirty lines, whose
//   stores never reach the PSRAM. The CPU's soft reset doesn't reset the cache: dirty lines
//   survive it, and no transfer is in flight then (the GPIO store that starts it completed
//   outside the window, after its fetch).
pub module soc_dcache (
    clk  : input clock,
    rst  : input reset,
    clear: input logic,

    // CPU side
    rd_idx    : input  logic<9> , // data_addr[10:2]: the word of the access, from EXECUTE on
    data_req  : input  logic    , // the CPU has a data access on the bus (unified_cpu)
    data_sel  : input  logic    , // data_addr is in the window
    data_addr : input  logic<21>, // data_waddr[22:2]: the PSRAM word of the registered access address
    data_we   : input  logic    , // 1: store, 0: load
    data_wdata: input  logic<32>,
    data_wstrb: input  logic<4> ,
    data_ready: output logic    ,
    rdata     : output logic<32>, // the loaded word, valid when a window load completes
    hit       : output logic    ,

    // soc_xmem_bridge's data side: the line transfers, one word a request
    mem_sel  : output logic    ,
    mem_we   : output logic    ,
    mem_addr : output logic<21>, // the PSRAM word
    mem_wdata: output logic<32>,
    mem_wstrb: output logic<4> ,
    mem_ready: input  logic    ,
    mem_rdata: input  logic<32>,

    // soc_icache's probe: its miss at the PSRAM word of the fetch (pc_reg[22:2])
    probe_req  : input  logic    ,
    probe_addr : input  logic<21>,
    probe_dirty: output logic    , // the line holding probe_addr is dirty: soc_icache's fill_hold
) {
    const LINES : u32 = soc_pkg::DCACHE_LINES;
    const NWORDS: u32 = LINES * 8;

    enum State {
        IDLE,
        WB,
        FILL,
    }

    var tags : logic<14> [LINES] ; // {valid, dirty, addr[22:11]}
    var words: logic<36> [NWORDS]; // {the bytes stored since the fill, the word}

    var tag_q    : logic<14>;
    var word_q   : logic<36>;
    var rd_idx_q : logic<9> ;
    var stale_q  : logic    ;
    var swept    : logic    ;
    var sweep_idx: logic<6> ;
    var state    : State    ;
    var is_probe : logic    ; // the write-back is the probe's: back to IDLE after it
    var primed   : logic    ; // in WB: word_q holds word cnt
    var cnt      : logic<3> ; // the word being transferred
    var line_r   : logic<6> ; // the line being transferred
    var tag_r    : logic<12>; // and the tag of its words in the PSRAM

    let idx : logic<9>  = data_addr[8:0];
    let line: logic<6>  = data_addr[8:3];
    let tag : logic<12> = data_addr[20:9];
    let win : logic     = data_req && data_sel;
    let idle: logic     = state == State::IDLE;

    // The registered tag and word are this access's
    let lookup: logic = win && swept && idle && !stale_q && rd_idx_q == idx;
    let match : logic = tag_q[13] && tag_q[11:0] == tag;

    assign hit        = lookup && match;
    assign data_ready = !win || hit;
    assign rdata      = word_q[31:0];

    let miss        : logic = lookup && !match;
    let victim_dirty: logic = tag_q[13] && tag_q[12];

    let ptag: logic<14> = tags[probe_addr[8:3]];

    assign probe_dirty = swept && ptag[13] && ptag[12] && ptag[11:0] == probe_addr[20:9];

    let probe_wb: logic = idle && swept && !win && probe_req && probe_dirty;

    assign mem_sel   = state == State::FILL || state == State::WB && primed;
    assign mem_we    = state == State::WB;
    assign mem_addr  = {tag_r, line_r, cnt};
    assign mem_wdata = word_q[31:0];
    assign mem_wstrb = word_q[35:32];

    let done    : logic    = mem_sel && mem_ready;
    let last    : logic    = done && cnt == 3'd7;
    let cnt_next: logic<3> = cnt + {2'b00, done};
    let ra      : logic<9> = if state == State::WB ? {line_r, cnt_next} : rd_idx;

    let merge: logic<32> = {
        if data_wstrb[3] ? data_wdata[31:24] : word_q[31:24], if data_wstrb[2] ? data_wdata[23:16] : word_q[23:16],
        if data_wstrb[1] ? data_wdata[15:8] : word_q[15:8], if data_wstrb[0] ? data_wdata[7:0] : word_q[7:0]
    };

    var tag_we    : logic    ;
    var tag_waddr : logic<6> ;
    var tag_wdata : logic<14>;
    var word_we   : logic    ;
    var word_waddr: logic<9> ;
    var word_wdata: logic<36>;

    always_comb {
        tag_we     = 1'b0;
        tag_waddr  = line_r;
        tag_wdata  = {2'b10, tag_r};
        word_we    = 1'b0;
        word_waddr = {line_r, cnt};
        word_wdata = {4'b0000, mem_rdata};
        if !swept {
            tag_we    = clear;
            tag_waddr = sweep_idx;
            tag_wdata = 14'd0;
        } else if hit && data_we {
            // store hit: merge the bytes, record them, the line is dirty
            tag_we     = 1'b1;
            tag_waddr  = line;
            tag_wdata  = {2'b11, tag};
            word_we    = 1'b1;
            word_waddr = idx;
            word_wdata = {word_q[35:32] | data_wstrb, merge};
        } else if state == State::FILL && done {
            // a word of the fill; after the last, the line is valid and clean
            word_we = 1'b1;
            tag_we  = last;
        } else if state == State::WB && last && is_probe {
            // the probe's write-back is over: the line stays valid, now clean
            tag_we = 1'b1;
        }
    }

    always_ff (clk) {
        if tag_we {
            tags[tag_waddr] = tag_wdata;
        }
        tag_q = tags[rd_idx[8:3]];
    }

    always_ff (clk) {
        if word_we {
            words[word_waddr] = word_wdata;
        }
        word_q = words[ra];
    }

    always_ff (clk, rst) {
        if_reset {
            swept     = 1'b0;
            sweep_idx = 6'd0;
            rd_idx_q  = 9'd0;
            stale_q   = 1'b0;
            state     = State::IDLE;
            is_probe  = 1'b0;
            primed    = 1'b0;
            cnt       = 3'd0;
            line_r    = 6'd0;
            tag_r     = 12'd0;
        } else {
            if !swept && clear {
                sweep_idx = sweep_idx + 6'd1;
                if sweep_idx == 6'd63 {
                    swept = 1'b1;
                }
            }
            rd_idx_q = rd_idx;
            stale_q  = !idle || tag_we && tag_waddr == rd_idx[8:3] || word_we && word_waddr == rd_idx;
            cnt      = cnt_next;
            case state {
                State::IDLE: {
                    if miss {
                        line_r   = line;
                        is_probe = 1'b0;
                        if victim_dirty {
                            state = State::WB;
                            tag_r = tag_q[11:0];
                        } else {
                            state = State::FILL;
                            tag_r = tag;
                        }
                    } else if probe_wb {
                        state    = State::WB;
                        line_r   = probe_addr[8:3];
                        tag_r    = probe_addr[20:9];
                        is_probe = 1'b1;
                    }
                }
                State::WB: {
                    primed = !last;
                    if last {
                        if is_probe {
                            state = State::IDLE;
                        } else {
                            state = State::FILL;
                            tag_r = tag;
                        }
                    }
                }
                default: {
                    if last {
                        state = State::IDLE;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
